{
  "title": "Medial Clavicle Physeal Fracture",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4123/medial-clavicle-physeal-fracture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 12 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Medial Clavicle Physeal Fractures, also known pseudodislocation of the sternoclavicular joint, are rare injuries to the medial physis of the clavicle in children.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with serendipity radiographic views but CT scan is the study of choice to differentiate from sternoclavicular dislocations.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally nonoperative management. Rarely, surgical management is indicated with posterior displacement associated with airway or neurovascular compromise.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**rare injury**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fall onto an outstretched extremity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "direct blow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "child abuse a rare cause",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "considered a childhood equivalent to **adult sternoclavicular separation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "physeal sleeve and strong costoclavicular and sternoclavicular ligaments usually remain intact with injury . However, in series by Lee et al. of 40 patients treated operatively for a posterior sternoclavicular injury 50% were physeal fractures and 50% were actually sternoclavicular dislocations",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4123/images/injury_periosteum_intact.jpg",
                      "caption": "Periosteum intact"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anterior displacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "metaphyseal fragment may be sharp and palpable immediately beneath the skin",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "clavicular head of the sternocleidomastoid muscle is pulled anteriorly with the bone and spasms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patient's head may be tilted towards the affected side",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "posterior displacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "local swelling, tenderness, and depression of the medial end of the clavicle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**innominate artery and vein, internal jugular vein, phrenic and vagus nerves, trachea, and esophagus may be injured with posterior displacement**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4123/images/nuerovascular_structures.jpg",
                          "caption": "Vascular structures"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Clavicle osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "S-shaped bone whose medial end is connected to the axial skeleton via the sternoclavicular joint and lateral end is connected to the scapula via the acromioclavicular joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Clavicle ossification",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "overview",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**first bone to ossify** in the fifth week in utero",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "central clavicle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "initial growth (<5 years) occurs from the ossification center in the central portion of the clavicle (intramembranous ossification)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "distal clavicle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "continued growth occurs at the medial and lateral epiphyseal plates",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral epiphysis does not ossify until age 18 years",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "medial clavicle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**approximately 80% of clavicular growth occurs at the medial physis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "does not begin to ossify until 18 to 20 years",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**last physis to close in the body (20-25yrs)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "sternoclavicular dislocations in teenagers/young adults may actually be physeal fracture-dislocations",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dysfunction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**anterior dislocation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "deformity with a palpable bump",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**posterior dislocations**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dyspnea or **dysphagia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tachypnea and **stridor**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**diminution or absence of distal pulses**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**paresthesias or paresis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "prominence that increases with arm abduction and elevation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ROM and instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**decreased arm ROM**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**paresthesias** in affected upper extremity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "venous congestion or diminished pulse when compared with the contralateral side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "difficult to visualize on AP, and radiographs usually unreliable to assess for fracture and degree of displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4123/images/xray_medial_clavicle.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**serendipity views** ( beam at 40 deg cephalic tilt)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4123/images/seren.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "anterior displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "the affected clavicle is above the contralateral clavicle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "posterior displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "the affected clavicle is below the contralateral clavicle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Axial CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4123/images/22_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4123/images/3d_recon_medial_clavicle.jpg",
              "caption": "CT 3d medial clavicle"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "is the study of choice",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can differentiate from **sternoclavicular dislocations**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can visualize mediastinal structures and injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**most asymptomatic injuries**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "will remodel and do not require intervention as the periosteal sleeve is intact",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4123/images/remodeling.jpg",
                              "caption": "Remodeling"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**anterior displacement**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "have good functional results treated nonoperatively",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**posterior displacement**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "if no injury to mediastinal structures",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction under anesthesia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**acute posterior displacement with** airway, esophageal, or neurovascular compromise",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "contraindications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "late presenting posterior dislocations",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "closed reduction not attempted as medial clavicle may be adherent to vascular structures in the mediastinum",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "open reduction internal fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**failure of closed reduction with continued symptoms**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**chronic symptomatic posterior dislocations**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "postreduction management",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "obtain CT to confirm stability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed reduction in the operating room under anesthesia**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "thoracic surgeon available",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**anterior dislocation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "patient placed supine with a bolster under shoulders",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "longitudinal traction to both upper extremities and gentle posterior pressure to medial metaphyseal fragment applied",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "medial fragment may be grasped with a towel clip to help facilitate reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "if unsuccessful, usually treated in a sling",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**posterior dislocation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "patient placed supine position with a bolster under shoulders",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "longitudinal traction applied to arm with the shoulder adducted",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "a posteriorly directed force is applied to the shoulder while the medial end of the clavicle is grasped with a towel clip and brought anteriorly",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "if reduction fails, proceed to open reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Open Reduction Internal Fixation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "horizontal incision the over superior/medial clavicle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "towel clip to reduce",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "sutures from medial clavicle to sternum/medial epiphysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**sutures preferred as may allow for MRI in the future**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pin fixation should be avoided due to danger of migration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Persistent instability**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "incidence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rare in children as they have a high propensity to remodel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Laceration of subclavian artery or vein**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "incidence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rare",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**suggested by rapidly expanding hematoma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "thick periosteum usually protective",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "repair of vessel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Pin migration**",
          "table": null,
